   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "1 \u00b7 Description"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Each of the six new reports has a "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Location",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " chooser in its toolbar, so a person can pick which branch or branches the report covers."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "If somebody only has access to "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "one",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " branch, that chooser has nothing to choose. There is only ever one answer. The product owner has decided the chooser should simply not be shown to that person."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Right now it "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "is",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " shown \u2014 on "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "all six",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " reports. The person sees a control reading "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "\"Location \u2014 All locations\"",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "em"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": ", with a clear button and a dropdown arrow, that cannot change anything about what they see."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Why it matters:",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " it is a control that does nothing, offered to the people least able to make sense of it. It reads as though there is more data available somewhere and they have filtered it out, which prompts support questions. It is also the one place in the six reports where the product disagrees with the product owner's decision about who sees the location controls at all."
    }
   ]
  },
